  "nl_text": "The rschema_0071 database is designed to manage information about mines and their safety inspections. The mine table stores details about each mine, including its unique number, name, location, and the person in charge, which is linked to the safety officer table through a foreign key. The safety officer table contains information about each safety officer, such as their number, name, gender, telephone number, position, and the mine they are in charge of, with the mine number referencing the mine table. The safety inspection record table stores records of safety inspections, including the inspection date, content, results, and the inspector, with the mine number referencing the mine table and forming a composite primary key with the inspection date.",
  "gold_question": "Business requirement description: A non-metallic mining company has multiple mines, and each mine has multiple safety officers. The safety officer has information such as safety officer number, name, gender, telephone number, and position. The mine has information such as mine number, name, location, and person in charge. During each safety inspection, it is necessary to record the inspection date, inspection content, inspection results, and inspector information. The information system needs to be able to perform statistical analysis on the safety inspection situation of the mine.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0071.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0071\nCREATE TABLE `mine` (\n  `mine_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`mine_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `mine_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`person_in_charge`) REFERENCES `safety_officer` (`officer_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `safety_officer` (\n  `officer_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `telephone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mine_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`officer_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `safety_officer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`mine_number`) REFERENCES `mine` (`mine_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `safety_inspection_record` (\n  `inspection_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `mine_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `results` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `inspector` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`mine_number`, `inspection_date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `safety_inspection_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`mine_number`) REFERENCES `mine` (`mine_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
